From e0a204ff613648d4d424bebb92b232e79569a7c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <m.seyfarth@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 16:59:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] i686: x87 top-of-stack cache for F64 binop chains;
 reversed RR forms in the assembler

emit_float_binop lowered every F64 binop as load/load/f..p/fstpl: both
operands reloaded from their slots and the result stored back, with the
x87 stack empty between instructions. FP expression trees therefore
paid two loads and one store per node (fp_kernel inner loop: 46 fld /
23 fst vs GCC's 16/8 on identical arithmetic) and the census showed the
FP-staging disease (nbody 3.78x of GCC) across all i686 FP code.

Add the x87 twin of the vector deferred-store mechanism:

- compute_x87_defer_values (stack_layout analysis): F64 binop results
  whose single use is an operand of the immediately-following F64 binop
  in the same block. Adjacency + single-use makes the deferral sound by
  construction: nothing can observe the slot or touch the x87 stack
  inside the window.

- emit_f64_binop_tracked: when the previous binop left its result on
  st(0) (non-popping fstl, slot already correct), the consumer dups the
  register copy for a square (fld %st(0)), consumes it in place as lhs
  (f{add,subr,mul,divr} %st(1), %st + fstp %st(1)), as rhs
  (f{add,sub,mul,div} %st(1), %st + fstp %st(1)), or pops it before
  building an unrelated pair. The result itself stays on the stack via
  fstl exactly when the analysis proved the next binop consumes it.

- Soundness cage: state.x87_pending tracks the cached copy;
  CodegenState::emit/emit_fmt flush it before any foreign x87 line or
  label (central x87_pre_emit hook; emit! macro rerouted through
  CodegenState); block boundaries call the new flush_x87_pending trait
  hook; calls, returns, and inline asm flush explicitly (x87 is
  caller-saved / template-opaque). x87_suppress keeps the hook inert
  inside the binop's own controlled sequences. FP-stack depth is
  therefore bounded by construction and the slot copy stays correct
  for ordinary memory readers.

- i686 assembler: add the missing reversed non-popping register forms
  fsubr/fdivr (D8 /5, /7) with the DC direction swap for the
  %st, %st(i) operand order; register them in the mnemonic table.

Validation: fpdiff.c (all 10 shape x operator combinations, sub/div in
both directions, squares, 64 value sets) is bit-exact against gcc -m32
-O2 and -O0; i686 corpus 443 pass / 79 known fails / 13 skip-compare
with the failure set identical to the pre-change baseline; x86-64
corpus 524/0/11; lib tests 1306/0/6 with -D warnings.
